From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nate Isern <nate@oxy.so>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make Astro's Mojo interfaces reachable from its own pages

A WebUI controller that implements a Mojo interface and overrides
`BindInterface` for it is still unreachable until the interface appears in the
frame binder map: `RenderFrameHostImpl` looks the interface up there, finds
nothing, and drops the request. The page sees a pipe that never answers. There
is no error, on either side.

This registers Astro's two interfaces for `astro://settings`, and registers
them SEPARATELY rather than as one, because they are not the same grant:

  astro.mojom.ThemeProvider              read-only. Every Astro page binds it,
                                         so the theme is live everywhere -- new
                                         tab page, side panels, settings.

  astro.settings.mojom.PageHandlerFactory  writes the theme. Granted here to
                                         the settings controller alone, which
                                         is also the only surface holding the
                                         settingsPrivate grant (patch 060).

A single read-write interface would have made every page that wants to READ
the theme able to CHANGE it, which is a grant nobody would have written down
deliberately.

Registered in the desktop parts file, not the all-platforms one, to match
where `AstroSettingsUIConfig` itself is registered: inside the non-Android
branch of chrome_web_ui_configs.cc. The `//chrome/browser` dependency on
`//chrome/browser/oxy:webui_controllers` is in the same non-Android branch and
covers both halves of what this file needs -- the controller's own header, and
the generated mojom headers, which arrive through that target's `public_deps`
on `//chrome/browser/oxy/webui:mojo_bindings` and must EXIST before this file
compiles, not merely link afterwards.

Owned by https://github.com/OxyHQ/Astro/issues/15.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/BUILD.gn
@@ -4255,6 +4255,7 @@ static_library("browser") {
       "//chrome/browser/media/router/discovery/access_code:access_code_sink_service",
       "//chrome/browser/metrics/desktop_session_duration",
       "//chrome/browser/new_tab_page/chrome_colors",
+      "//chrome/browser/oxy:webui_controllers",
       "//chrome/browser/page_content_annotations:fetcher",
       "//chrome/browser/password_manager/password_change",
       "//chrome/browser/performance_manager/public/user_tuning",
diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_browser_interface_binders_webui_parts_desktop.cc
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/new_tab_page/modules/v2/most_relevant_tab_resumption/most_relevant_tab_resumption.mojom.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/new_tab_page/modules/v2/tab_groups/tab_groups.mojom.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/new_tab_page/new_tab_page_util.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_settings.mojom.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_settings_ui.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/oxy/webui/astro_theme.mojom.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/lens/lens_overlay_untrusted_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/lens/lens_side_panel_untrusted_ui.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/omnibox/omnibox_next_features.h"
@@ -597,6 +600,20 @@ void PopulateChromeWebUIFrameBindersPartsDesktop(
         DefaultBrowserModalUI>(map);
   }
 #endif
+
+  // Astro's own typed transports. Without an entry in this map the interface
+  // is unreachable from the page: the controller's BindInterface is never
+  // called and the request is dropped, which the page sees as a pipe that
+  // never answers rather than as a missing registration.
+  //
+  // The two are granted separately and to different scopes on purpose.
+  // ThemeProvider is READ-only and every Astro page gets it; PageHandler
+  // WRITES the theme and is granted here only to the settings controller,
+  // which is also the only surface holding the settingsPrivate grant.
+  RegisterWebUIControllerInterfaceBinder<astro::mojom::ThemeProvider,
+                                         astro::AstroSettingsUI>(map);
+  RegisterWebUIControllerInterfaceBinder<
+      astro::settings::mojom::PageHandlerFactory, astro::AstroSettingsUI>(map);
 }
 
 void PopulateChromeWebUIFrameInterfaceBrokersTrustedPartsDesktop(
